# RubyLLM Tools — this repo pins ruby_llm 1.11.0

The docs at https://rubyllm.com/tools/ describe the latest version. **Check `Gemfile.lock` and the
installed gem source before using an API from the docs.** Known differences in 1.11:

- Use `description '...'` — the `desc` class-method alias does not exist yet.
- Callbacks are `chat.on_tool_call { |tool_call| }` and `chat.on_tool_result { |result| }`
  (not `before_tool_call`/`after_tool_result`). `on_tool_result` does NOT receive the tool name.
- No signature inference: every argument needs a `param` (flat) or `params do ... end` (nested) declaration.
- No `choice:`/`calls:`/`concurrency:` options on `with_tools`; tools execute sequentially.
- **`execute_tool` has no rescue**: an exception raised inside a tool propagates out of
  `chat.complete` and kills the whole turn. Tools must catch their own errors (see below).
- Tool names derive from the class name with `_tool` suffix stripped, but module namespaces leak in
  (`Assistant::FooTool` → `assistant--foo`). Override `#name` for namespaced tools.
- Hash return values are stored via `to_s`; return a JSON string for a clean model-facing payload.

## Defining a tool

```ruby
class ConversationList < RubyLLM::Tool
  description 'Lists inbox conversations, filterable by status and interest'

  param :interest_status, desc: 'One of: interested, meeting_request, not_interested, wrong_person',
        required: false
  param :limit, type: :integer, desc: 'Max results (default 20, max 50)', required: false

  def execute(interest_status: nil, limit: 20)
    # ...
  end
end
```

- Tools may define `initialize` for dependencies (account/organization context) —
  register the *instance*: `chat.with_tool(ConversationList.new(account:))`.
- Attach with `chat.with_tools(a, b)`; streaming blocks pass through tool rounds, so post-tool
  text still streams.

## Error handling (per official docs, adapted to this app)

- **Recoverable** (bad arguments, record not found, empty query): return `{ error: '...' }` —
  the model sees the error and can correct itself or explain to the user.
- **Unauthorized / cross-org ID**: return the same "not found" error as a missing record.
  Never reveal that a record exists in another organization.
- **Infrastructure failures** (`ActiveRecord::ConnectionNotEstablished`, `StatementInvalid`,
  `PG::Error`): rescue in the shared base tool class, `Rails.logger.error(...)` with class +
  message, and return `{ error: 'This tool is temporarily unavailable...' }` so the turn completes
  gracefully instead of crashing the stream (mandatory in 1.11 — see execute_tool note above).
- Never let a raw exception message or backtrace reach the model or the user.

## Security (mandatory in this repo)

- Treat every `execute` argument as untrusted user input — the LLM generates them.
- Inject account/organization via `initialize`, NEVER from tool arguments.
- Every query goes through `Pundit.policy_scope!(account, Model)` AND is scoped to the chat's
  organization. Mutations call `Pundit.authorize(account, record, :action?)`.
- Policies read `Current.organization` / `Current.organization_membership` — background jobs must
  wrap tool-using LLM calls in `Current.set(...)` or every scope fails closed to none.
- A foreign-org ID must behave as "not found" — use `find_by(id:)` on the scoped relation.
- No `eval`/`send`/`system`/SQL interpolation with tool arguments. Use
  `ActiveRecord::Base.sanitize_sql_like` for ILIKE terms. Validate enums against allow-lists.
- Cap every `limit`/`offset` argument server-side regardless of what the model sends.
